      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The client's AeroFlow Dynamics design introduces a high-efficiency micro-channel cooling system with a unique lattice structure that distinguishes it from standard cooling holes described in US Patent 9,123,456. While US Patent 10,456,789 also utilizes lattice-based cooling, the new invention achieves superior thermal dissipation through specific engineering improvements not evident in that prior art. Unlike US Patent 11,222,333, which relies solely on external heat resistance, this innovation integrates internal active cooling mechanisms entirely within the blade structure. This combination of novel geometry and enhanced performance metrics establishes a clear novelty threshold for the application.",
      "source": "target",
